151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (WhatNext Vision Motors is a Salesforce-based CRM project created to manage the main activities of an automotive dealership in one place. Instead of keeping vehicle, customer, dealer, order, test-drive, and service information separately, the project brings these records together inside a single Lightning application.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (The project was designed around a simple dealership workflow. Staff can add vehicles and maintain their stock details, register customers, manage dealers, create vehicle orders, schedule test drives, and record service requests. Relationships between these records make it easier to move from one activity to another without repeatedly entering the same information. Automation was added for the parts of the process that would otherwise require repeated manual work. For example, the system checks vehicle stock before an order is confirmed, assigns a dealer through Flow when an order is created, and sends a reminder before a scheduled test drive. Apex is used where programmatic logic is needed, while Salesforce configuration features handle the remaining business requirements.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (The application is presented through Salesforce Lightning pages, with separate tabs and organized record layouts. Reports and dashboards are also used to give users a quick view of stock, orders, and test-drive activity.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
