228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Flow was used to automate repetitive activities in the WhatNext Vision Motors application. Instead of requiring users to perform every step manually, the configured flows respond to specific record events and carry out the required actions automatically. Two record-triggered flows were developed for the project. The first flow handles dealer assignment when a new vehicle order is created, while the second flow sends a reminder email before a scheduled test drive. These automations help reduce manual work and make the dealership workflow more systematic.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (A validation rule was added to make sure that a vehicle order is confirmed only when the selected vehicle has sufficient stock. Before completing the order, Salesforce checks the available stock quantity of the associated vehicle. If the stock quantity is zero, the user is prevented from confirming the order and the configured error message is displayed. This helps avoid orders being created for vehicles that are currently unavailable and keeps the order information consistent with the vehicle inventory.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
