/P 140 0 R
/T (7.3 Troubleshooting Approach)
/E (7.3 Troubleshooting Approach)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (When an issue occurs, the problem is first identified and reproduced with controlled data. The related object, fields, validation rules, Flow, permissions, or Apex logic are then reviewed. Logs are checked where required, the cause is corrected, and the original scenario is tested again. After the fix works as expected, the corrected configuration can be deployed to the required environment.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 140 0 R
/T (8. Conclusion)
/E (8. Conclusion)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The WhatNext Vision Motors project brings the main activities of an automotive dealership into one Salesforce CRM application. The project connects vehicles, customers, dealers, orders, test drives, and service requests so that related information can be managed together instead of being handled separately. Stock validation helps prevent incorrect order confirmation, Flow automates dealer assignment and test-drive reminders, and Apex supports the order-processing logic that requires programmatic control. Lightning pages, reports, dashboards, and Salesforce security features make the system more organized and easier to manage. Overall, the project provided practical experience in combining Salesforce configuration features such as Objects, Fields, Relationships, Validation Rules, Flow, Reports, and Dashboards with Apex classes and triggers to build a CRM solution around a real automotive dealership workflow.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
